## RESULTS
Our construct for incorporating nanocrystals of MOFs into supercapacitors is illustrated in Scheme 1. It is based on a coin-type device composed of films made from nMOFs doped with graphene. The films are placed on both sides of a separator membrane and soaked by a solution of an electrolyte. It is expected that by charging the device, the positive and negative ions of the electrolyte move in opposite directions through the separator and into the MOF pores. During discharge, the ions migrate out of the pores and the electrons flow out of the device. MOFs would perform
