## METHODS
Preparation of nMOFs. Detailed synthetic procedures for all nMOFs are described in the Supporting Information. Here, we describe the preparation method for nHKUST-1, representatively. A $126~\mathsf{m g}$ portion of 1,3,5-benzenetricarboxylic acid $({\mathsf{B T C H}}_{3})$ and $0.25~\mathrm{mL}$ of triethylamine were dissolved in $2m L$ of $\mathbf{\xi}_{N,N}$ -dimethylformamide (DMF), while $215~\mathrm{mg}$ of ${\mathsf{C u}}(\mathsf{O A c})_{2}$ 3 ${\sf H}_{2}{\sf O}$ was dissolved in $5m L$ of DMF. The solutions of 1,3,5- benzenetricarboxylic acid and $\mathsf{C u}(\mathsf{O A c})_{2}{\cdot}\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O}$ was combined in a mixture of DMF $\mathrm{78~mL)}$ ), EtOH $(25~\mathsf{m L})$ , and ${\mathsf{H}}_{2}{\mathsf{O}}$ $25~\mathrm{mL}$ ) and stirred vigorously for $1\ h$ at ambient temperature. The resultant nHKUST-1 was washed twice with DMF using a centrifuge (9000 rpm for $20\mathrm{\min})$ and sonication and then sequentially immersed in acetone for three $24\mathrm{~h~}$ periods. Finally, nHKUST-1 was activated by removing the solvent under vacuum overnight.
Preparation of nMOF Films. A $70~\mathsf{m g}$ portion of the nMOF was mixed and dispersed with $53\mu\mathrm{L}$ of oleic acid in $4.6~\mathrm{mL}$ of hexane (nMOF/hexane dispersion) by sonication for $3h$ . At the same time, graphene layers $(0.5\mathrm{mg}\mathrm{mL}^{-1}.$ ) were separated in hexane by using a tip-sonic processor for a total of 40 min $(4\times10$ min operation)
and continuously sonicated in the ultrasonic bath $(40k H z)$ to keep their dispersion (graphene/hexane dispersion). After the nMOF was separated from $1\ m L$ of nMOF/hexane dispersion using a centrifuge (9000 rpm, $10~\mathrm{min}$ ), it was redispersed in $1m L$ of graphene/hexane dispersion $(0.5\mathrm{\mg\mL^{-1}})$ ) to make a nMOF and graphene dispersion in hexane (nMOF/graphene/hexane dispersion). In the meantime, substrates were cleaned with hypophosphorous acid (50 wt $\%$ solution in water) for 1 h after washing with acetone, ethanol, and water. The nMOF/graphene/hexane dispersion was coated on the cleaned substrates in the spin coater (7000 rpm, 2 min) to give a $2\mu\mathsf{m}$ thickness of nMOF film. Oleic acid was removed by immersing the nMOF film in acetone, drying with nitrogen flow, and outgassing at room temperature for $12\mathsf{h}$ All processes were done in succession.
Fabrication of Supercapacitors. For the fabrication of supercapacitors, two nMOF film samples, separator and electrolyte, were assembled in a coin-shaped cell. Specifically, two pieces of nMOF film $(2\mu\mathsf{m})$ on Ti substrates $(25\mu\mathsf{m})$ ) were sandwiched with a separator (monolayer polypropylene separator membranes, thickness $25\ \mu\mathsf{m},$ Celgard) and soaked in $1.0~\mathsf{M}$ of tetraethylammonium tetrafluoroborate $(C_{2}H_{5})_{4}N B F_{4})$ in acetonitrile. After the coin-shaped cell was sealed, supercapacitors were electrochemically tested using galvanostatic and cyclic voltammetry measurements. The same method was applied for all of the supercapacitors in this paper.
